<h2>Row Select</h2>
<p>Select table rows with checkboxes — select-all, shift-click range select, and a bulk-actions bar that appears once anything is selected.</p>

<div class="demo-box" data-controller="row-select">
  <div data-row-select-target="bar" hidden>
    <strong><span data-row-select-target="count"></span> selected</strong>
    <button
      type="button"
      onclick="this.closest('[data-controller=row-select]').querySelectorAll('[data-row-select-target=row]:checked').forEach((cb) => cb.closest('tr').remove()); this.closest('[data-row-select-target=bar]').hidden = true;"
    >
      Delete selected
    </button>
  </div>

  <table>
    <caption>
      Click a row checkbox to select it, shift-click another to select the
      range between them, or use the header checkbox to select all.
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            data-row-select-target="all"
            data-action="change->row-select#toggleAll"
            aria-label="Select all rows"
          />
        </th>
        <th scope="col">Name</th>
        <th scope="col">Role</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            data-row-select-target="row"
            data-action="click->row-select#toggle"
            aria-label="Select Alice"
          />
        </td>
        <td>Alice</td>
        <td>Engineer</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            data-row-select-target="row"
            data-action="click->row-select#toggle"
            aria-label="Select Bob"
          />
        </td>
        <td>Bob</td>
        <td>Designer</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            data-row-select-target="row"
            data-action="click->row-select#toggle"
            aria-label="Select Charlie"
          />
        </td>
        <td>Charlie</td>
        <td>Product Manager</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            data-row-select-target="row"
            data-action="click->row-select#toggle"
            aria-label="Select Dana"
          />
        </td>
        <td>Dana</td>
        <td>Engineer</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            data-row-select-target="row"
            data-action="click->row-select#toggle"
            aria-label="Select Erin"
          />
        </td>
        <td>Erin</td>
        <td>Support</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>
  "Delete selected" removes the checked rows directly from the page (this app
  has no database, so there's nothing to persist) — similar to how a Rails
  app might remove rows via a Turbo Stream after a real bulk-delete action.
  Selecting a row, deleting it, then shift-clicking another row afterward
  exercises the fix for a stale range anchor after a row disappears from
  under the controller.
</p>
